# Semgrep excludes tests by default which causes a behavior difference between
# using Semgrep via pre-commit (which explicitly passes the list of files, e.g.,
# `semgrep saleor/tests/test_foo.py`) instead of passing a directory (such as
# `semgrep ./saleor`) thus causing Semgrep to not ignore test files in pre-commit
# while running Semgrep manually outside pre-commit would exclude tests.
!**/tests/
!**/tests/**
